pthread.kext's private headers, copied from third_party/libpthread/kern/
(libpthread-454.80.2, the macos-112 pin) for bsd_pthread_synch.c, which is
that repo's kern/kern_synch.c (DAR-416). This kernel links the pthread
"kext" in directly; there is no kext build to supply libpthread's include
paths.

Copied unchanged except:
  kern_internal.h:46-47  "kern/synch_internal.h" / "kern/kern_trace.h"
                         -> "synch_internal.h" / "kern_trace.h" (same dir).
  kern_internal.h:29-30,209  include guard _SYS_PTHREAD_INTERNAL_H_ ->
                         _PTHREAD_KEXT_KERN_INTERNAL_H_: xnu's own
                         bsd/sys/pthread_internal.h uses the same guard.
                         With BSD_KERNEL_PRIVATE, sys/user.h:87-88 includes
                         it first and this whole header is skipped. The
                         object is now built without BSD_KERNEL_PRIVATE
                         (bsd/conf/Makefile.template), so the rename is
                         belt-and-braces.
  kern_internal.h:48-49  removed #include "pthread/qos.h" and
                         "pthread/qos_private.h" (libpthread's userland QoS
                         headers; nothing in these headers or in
                         kern_synch.c uses them -- the kernel QoS types come
                         from xnu's own <pthread/priority_private.h> and
                         <mach/thread_policy.h>).
  kern_internal.h:149     added `typedef unsigned int _pthread_set_flags_t;`
                         -- the type of the enum at libpthread
                         private/pthread/qos_private.h:62, needed only by
                         the _bsdthread_ctl_set_self prototype after the
                         include above was dropped.
bsd_pthread_synch.c differs from kern/kern_synch.c only in its three
#include "kern/..." lines (-> "pthread_kext/...").

Size note: the real struct ksyn_waitq_element here is 56 bytes on LP64;
xnu's opaque stand-in (bsd/sys/pthread_internal.h:35-41) reserves 48. It
lives in struct uthread's uu_save union (sys/user.h:130-190), whose
kevent member is larger, so it fits. Stock xnu-7195 has the same mismatch.
